y the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae9cc84-e109-5f7c-9f4d-b9b40e636dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477782} {:answer/id #uuid "5f33a7f4-47fb-5abe-88a3-e95d9751522c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477927} {:answer/id #uuid "6665977e-7139-5506-bb97-4e4bbe74c55d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477942} {:answer/id #uuid "6915c9ea-6ce2-572d-9bd8-64cef6be30b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477948} {:answer/id #uuid "e614ab4c-8a87-58b6-b80c-ac869525afec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ae9cc84-e109-5f7c-9f4d-b9b40e636dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477782} :answer-field/id #uuid "721111c4-d48e-525f-b4f4-04c7d19ba2d4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25637a16-a8f5-5685-8a0f-edf70d2d5668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477808} {:answer/id #uuid "84fee49e-7c03-53bd-a98c-0c5765cfdc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478009} {:answer/id #uuid "ce636da0-2c87-5f22-ac37-82c53190cec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478145} {:answer/id #uuid "d42d02ae-c11e-5f67-b5d2-d449d04a25be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478157} {:answer/id #uuid "eb39f7a3-a88a-52cd-9bec-9258eadb7eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84fee49e-7c03-53bd-a98c-0c5765cfdc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478009} :answer-field/id #uuid "b61e8ed5-7cc2-570f-81a8-5d5bf851fe9d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478329} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c129137-e1ee-53de-8e36-dc30161a29cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477784} {:answer/id #uuid "61b8ff50-f2e2-5101-80b6-75a757c523cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477935} {:answer/id #uuid "b036313e-46bd-5ba5-a4e7-e269d18ebe70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478078} {:answer/id #uuid "c24c9a8f-aa9f-558b-959c-4b5b14437367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478115} {:answer/id #uuid "f56e5c31-f78d-5c7c-974f-377dab093766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c129137-e1ee-53de-8e36-dc30161a29cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{6x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477784} :answer-field/id #uuid "e02bf417-0393-51e7-a383-3100f1d57255" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb143e45-7802-56af-9fb3-105326be7da5" :question/math-academy-id "q-337383" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y=-2.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+6{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-6x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-6x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-6x})}^{′}+6(u{e}^{-6x}) & =-2 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-6x}-6u{e}^{-6x}+6u{e}^{-6x} & =-2 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-6x}-\\cancel{6u{e}^{-6x}}+\\cancel{6u{e}^{-6x}} & =-2 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-6x} & =-2 \\\\ {u}^{′} & =-2{e}^{6x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =-2{e}^{6x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -2{e}^{6x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{6x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-6x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-6x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{6x}\\cdot {e}^{-6x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042294e8-3c22-56fe-8cd4-f95c525ab5c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477744} {:answer/id #uuid "508431a0-cdbe-5c36-b26e-8f3456ed43e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477899} {:answer/id #uuid "7fcf92a2-5cdb-5d33-990d-1a112cf7edea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478000} {:answer/id #uuid "a6fc93bc-59a8-5ea9-8e6a-dd6bd24f0a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478058} {:answer/id #uuid "ca221104-f9bf-546f-acd6-2f66a99c0d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-7x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fcf92a2-5cdb-5d33-990d-1a112cf7edea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478000} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ccad504-1e12-599a-a42c-f450901d78aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478265} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cb152c-cade-5eda-a697-0d47b6838e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477742} {:answer/id #uuid "11ce2d34-f800-5cea-8179-d6056d875527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477765} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec5384b-5001-5210-9214-f09dc7d653a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478042} {:answer/id #uuid "bb0872e5-10fc-5af9-9728-8ce5eeb006f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb0872e5-10fc-5af9-9728-8ce5eeb006f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478100} :answer-field/id #uuid "60679c32-dd24-5bdf-abdd-97d73736289d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "542d0d08-8566-5b6f-9825-eff2afb91bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477911} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5c3ddf-bf8c-573c-bb65-7feb3acd26b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4x}\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478036} {:answer/id #uuid "c64e5492-8752-5936-adef-185caf3a66ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4x}\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478128} {:answer/id #uuid "f3d1b648-0c2d-5203-bc7b-1f53c350fa66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}\\int {e}^{-4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c64e5492-8752-5936-adef-185caf3a66ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4x}\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478128} :answer-field/id #uuid "e04727ea-c9aa-5634-9723-1114edbde733" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6273365a-c573-57e8-b4f1-3ec205edd4d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-337387" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-4x})}^{′}+4(u{e}^{-4x}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-4u{e}^{-4x}+4u{e}^{-4x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-\\cancel{4u{e}^{-4x}}+\\cancel{4u{e}^{-4x}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-4x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-4x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-4x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{-4x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-4x}\\int {e}^{4x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "497197b8-8e76-53b8-86a4-754349398785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477880} {:answer/id #uuid "6b46c7a3-36fa-593b-b8a4-fd59ab9a5bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477957} {:answer/id #uuid "9d326a77-95d4-5330-b18b-381ab039df29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478038} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6289c4-f3fa-56b7-a00e-e7a24c495194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478197} {:answer/id #uuid "f83737fd-3f7f-562a-8be3-3d48018765df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea6289c4-f3fa-56b7-a00e-e7a24c495194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478197} :answer-field/id #uuid "1201467f-65cf-51f2-8aac-3e057e5d3832" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52baabc1-e1ba-5e29-b8f3-ad0c45dac74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^